-- `add(...$initializers)` is fluent and accepts the same configuration objects, PSR-11 containers, service providers, and class strings as `ContainerFactory::create()`.
-- Each `build()` creates fresh aggregate, provider/config adapters, and autowiring state. Later registrations affect future builds only.
-- Supplied source objects are reused, including external containers and their own state. Class-string initializers are instantiated anew during each build.
-- `ContainerFactory::create()` delegates to the Builder, preserving a single assembly implementation. `container()` continues delegating to the Factory.
-- Source precedence, cross-source dependencies, lazy service resolution, optional nested configuration handling, and existing lifetime semantics are preserved.
-- PHPDoc, API/onboarding guides, README, and a runnable conditional-registration example document the new API.
