-FastForward Container v1.7.0 adds static container composition and corrects service-provider extension resolution.
 
-## Container composition
+### Added
 
-Use `ContainerFactory::create(...$initializers)` as an alternative to `container(...)`. The helper delegates to the same implementation. Each call creates a fresh aggregate, provider adapters, and autowiring container, while supplied PSR-11 container objects are reused.
+- Static composition through `ContainerFactory::create()`, sharing its assembly path with `container()`. ([#12](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/12))
+- Runnable provider/factory examples and expanded API, onboarding and integration documentation. ([#12](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/12))
 
-Unknown initializer class names and constructed objects that implement none of the supported initializer contracts raise `InvalidArgumentException`. Optional nested-configuration failures retain the existing handling policy.
+### Changed
 
-## Service-provider fixes
+- Shared test-status publication and Dependabot status handling. ([#8](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/8))
+- Native Pages reports and documentation publication. ([#9](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/9))
+- Contextual repository illustration. ([#7](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/7))
+- Documentation presentation and package/archive hygiene.
 
-- Extensions can supply an entry without a factory and receive `null` as the previous value.
-- Returned extension values replace the previous value, including scalars, arrays, and `null`; explicitly declared `void` extensions preserve the previous value for compatibility.
-- Successful resolutions cache the final value, including `null`.
-- Inferred concrete-class aliases preserve cached entries and callable factory/extension definitions registered for the same class ID in the provider container.
-- `has()` discovers callable factories and extensions without executing them, retaining short-circuit metadata lookup.
-- Provider discovery and execution failures are wrapped consistently, preserving the original exception. Textual exception codes remain available on that previous exception.
+### Fixed
 
-## Documentation and maintenance
+- Extension-only entries, including discovery without executing factories or extensions. ([#12](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/12))
+- Extension return values replacing the previous service, including `null`, while explicitly `void` extensions retain the previous value for compatibility. ([#12](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/12))
+- Cached null entries, concrete-class alias precedence and extension composition across providers. ([#12](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/12))
+- Preservation of provider discovery/execution failure causes, including textual exception codes on the previous exception. ([#12](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/12))
 
-- Expanded API, onboarding, integration, and provider documentation, with runnable examples for both construction styles.
-- Improved test-status publication, documentation reports, and package/archive hygiene since v1.6.0.
+### Security
 
-The delivery includes 109 tests and 264 assertions with 100% source coverage, validated on PHP 8.3, 8.4, and 8.5. The PHP requirement remains `^8.3`.
+- Ignore Composer CI environment dump files to prevent accidental inclusion in commits and distributions. ([#10](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/pull/10))
 
-The incremental `ContainerBuilder` proposal is tracked separately in [#13](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/issues/13). Transient lifetime design remains open in [#6](https://github.com/php-fast-forward/container/issues/6).
